NNAAMMEE
     cchhrroommeebbooookk__ppllaattffoorrmm — support driver for hardware on various Chromebook
     models

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines into
     the kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee cchhrroommeebbooookk__ppllaattffoorrmm

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           chromebook_platform_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The cchhrroommeebbooookk__ppllaattffoorrmm driver provides automatic configuration for de‐
     vices that cannot be enumerated or safely probed.  In particular, I2C pe‐
     ripherals are different from model to model.  cchhrroommeebbooookk__ppllaattffoorrmm has a
     model-specific information about the I2C peripherals, their drivers,
     their bus attachments and slave addresses.

     Note that cchhrroommeebbooookk__ppllaattffoorrmm does not load driver modules for the pe‐
     ripherals.  Those have to be compiled into the kernel or loaded sepa‐
     rately.

